      "review_notes": "The independent standard two-sided geometric law has atom coefficient(s,t)*exp(-s/t)^natAbs(z). Its analytic residue/quotient reindexing, reflected atoms, normalization and nonunit rates were independently reviewed and tested in Batch012. New continuation mathematics moves the exponential remainder test before independent geometric whole/sign draws and supplies one accepted-proposal conservation inequality for both retry sites. Main CTE follows that source order and returns the signed integer quotient or retries. Independent actual callers frame arbitrary signed-output credits and resources at generic rates, and explicitly instantiate rates2/3 and3/2. A negative-zero test with nonzero whole part confirms rejection happens after division; the positive sign retains F(0)."
    },
