      "review_notes": "The exact biased finite law counts source-word preimages under independently specified nearest/even binary rounding followed by modulus division. The mathematical rounding API gives quantum spacing, exact-fit and exact-divisible behavior, even midpoint ties and half-quantum error bounds with unbounded exponents. Main CTE composes deterministic exponentiation, a verified uniform binary word and deterministic rounding. Independent tests distinguish the precision3 map[0,0,1,2,2,3,4,4] from the precision6 unrounded map[0,0,1,1,2,3,3,4] for n5/width8, check masses1/4 and1/8 and infinite credit off the finite image, and verify midpoint20\u219216 versus28\u219232. Weak-language framed bit-length/rounding clients, zero-precision helper failure, zero-bit positive-precision singleton and arbitrary-resource main callers pass. No hardware IEEE or continuous-uniform claim is made."
    },
