      "review_notes": "The public target is the independently normalized UniformInt law. Pointwise finite-horizon credits describe retained states; the bulk interval identity already accepted with FYKY in Batch013 bounds the initial state by uniform output credit plus an exponentially vanishing cutoff tail. This lower orientation emits the first n ranks and recycles the upper residue. Main CTE follows one bit at a time, derives contradiction from cutoff credit1, and removes the horizon with an arbitrary positive error budget. Independent callers frame arbitrary ENNReal continuations and resources, exercise non-power-of-two bounds3 and5, check infinite off-support credit and use the singleton theorem without UniformInt. No individual retained state is assumed to have a uniform output law."
